-- A comparison slot ahead of the slot that point-recovers x = s1 / 3. The
-- comparison's indicator is a value, not a density: its path must not carry
-- x's recovery derivative, so p((True, 0.5)) = phi(0.5; 0, 3) = p((ANY, 0.5)).
-- It used to answer that / 3. Docs task
-- forwardchaining-path-derivative-includes-other-latents-jacobian.
p((True, 0.5))=(0.1311466, 1.0)
